{"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLNote","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLNote\/Kind-swift.struct"]]},"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlnote\/kind-swift.struct\/value"]}],"abstract":[{"text":"The value of this element.","type":"text"}],"primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"languages":["swift"],"tokens":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"let"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"value"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLNoteKindValue","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:7IvorMXL16MXLNoteKindValueO","text":"MXLNoteKindValue"}],"platforms":["macOS"]}],"kind":"declarations"}],"sections":[],"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLNote\/Kind-swift.struct\/value","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"metadata":{"title":"value","symbolKind":"property","modules":[{"name":"IvorMXL"}],"role":"symbol","roleHeading":"Instance Property","externalID":"s:7IvorMXL7MXLNoteV4KindV5valueAA0cD5ValueOvp","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"let"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"value"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:7IvorMXL16MXLNoteKindValueO","text":"MXLNoteKindValue"}]},"kind":"symbol","schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"major":0,"patch":0},"references":{"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLNote/Kind-swift.struct":{"type":"topic","title":"MXLNote.Kind","kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLNote\/Kind-swift.struct","abstract":[{"text":"The note-type type indicates the graphic note type. Values range from 1024th to maxima. The size attribute","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"indicates full, cue, grace-cue, or large size. The default is full for regular notes, grace-cue for notes that","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"contain both grace and cue elements, and cue for notes that contain either a cue or a grace element, but not","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"both.","type":"text"}],"role":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"Kind"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"Kind"}],"url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlnote\/kind-swift.struct"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLNote":{"fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"MXLNote","kind":"identifier"}],"title":"MXLNote","abstract":[{"text":"Notes are the most common type of MusicXML data. The MusicXML format distinguishes between elements used for","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"sound information and elements used for notation information (e.g., tie is used for sound, tied for notation).","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"Thus grace notes do not have a duration element. Cue notes have a duration element, as do forward elements,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"but no tie elements. Having these two types of information available can make interchange easier, as some","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"programs handle one type of information more readily than the other.","type":"text"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLNote","role":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlnote","kind":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"MXLNote","kind":"identifier"}],"type":"topic"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL":{"type":"topic","title":"IvorMXL","kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A MusicXML parser, normalizer, validator, and formatter."}],"role":"collection","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLNote/Kind-swift.struct/value":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLNote\/Kind-swift.struct\/value","title":"value","fragments":[{"text":"let","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"value","kind":"identifier"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"MXLNoteKindValue","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:7IvorMXL16MXLNoteKindValueO"}],"abstract":[{"text":"The value of this element.","type":"text"}],"type":"topic","kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlnote\/kind-swift.struct\/value","role":"symbol"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLNoteKindValue":{"title":"MXLNoteKindValue","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"enum"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLNoteKindValue"}],"kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlnotekindvalue","role":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"MXLNoteKindValue","kind":"identifier"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLNoteKindValue","abstract":[{"text":"The note-type-value type is used for the MusicXML type element and represents the graphic note type, from","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"1024th (shortest) to maxima (longest).","type":"text"}],"type":"topic"}}}